h1. Mainframe Knowledge Recovery — Business Rules (Draft)

{info:title=Review status}Every row below was extracted from a specific COBOL paragraph and carries its source citation. None of these are authoritative until an SME confirms or corrects them.{info}

h2. ACCTINQ

*Coverage:* 4 / 4 reachable paragraphs processed (100.0%)

||Rule ID||Paragraph||Citation||Business Rule||Status||
|ACCTINQ-A1|1000-READ-ACCOUNT|src/ACCTINQ.cbl:1000-READ-ACCOUNT|When a customer account inquiry is requested, the system looks up the account record; if no matching account is found, it displays an "ACCOUNT NOT FOUND" message and does not display any account details.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTINQ-A2|1000-READ-ACCOUNT|src/ACCTINQ.cbl:1000-READ-ACCOUNT|This account inquiry function is read-only: it only displays the current balance and status, and never updates account information.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTINQ-A3|2000-DISPLAY-BALANCE|src/ACCTINQ.cbl:2000-DISPLAY-BALANCE|When the account is found, the inquiry result displayed to the user includes the account identifier, the current account balance, and the account status.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|

----

h2. ACCTMSTR

*Coverage:* 20 / 20 reachable paragraphs processed (100.0%)

||Rule ID||Paragraph||Citation||Business Rule||Status||
|ACCTMSTR-A1|2100-READ-NEXT-ACCOUNT|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:2100-READ-NEXT-ACCOUNT|Only Savings and Checking are recognized account types; any other account type is logged as a data exception but the account still continues through processing.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A2|2200-VALIDATE-ACCOUNT-TYPE|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:2200-VALIDATE-ACCOUNT-TYPE|When an account's type is neither Savings nor Checking, the system displays a data exception message identifying the account, but does not stop processing it.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A3|3100-CALC-DAYS-SINCE-LAST-TRAN|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:3100-CALC-DAYS-SINCE-LAST-TRAN|The number of days since an account's last transaction is calculated by comparing today's date to the account's last transaction date.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A4|3200-MARK-DORMANT|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:3200-MARK-DORMANT|An active account with no transaction activity for more than 180 days is automatically reclassified as dormant.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A5|3300-CLOSE-LONG-DORMANT|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:3300-CLOSE-LONG-DORMANT|A dormant account with no transaction activity for more than 365 days is automatically closed by the system.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A6|3400-SET-FEE-CODE|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:3400-SET-FEE-CODE|For checking accounts, a fee code is assigned based on balance: accounts with a negative balance get an overdraft fee code, while accounts with a zero or positive balance get the standard fee code.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A7|3400-SET-FEE-CODE|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:3400-SET-FEE-CODE|The fee code must only ever be set for checking accounts; savings accounts share the same stored data location for their interest rate, so setting a fee code on a savings account would corrupt its recorded interest rate.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A8|4100-CHECK-FEE-WAIVER-MSTR|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:4100-CHECK-FEE-WAIVER-MSTR|The monthly maintenance fee is waived if the account balance is more than $500.00; if the balance is $500.00 or less, the fee is applied.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A9|4000-MONTHLY-FEE-PROCESSING|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:4000-MONTHLY-FEE-PROCESSING|Monthly maintenance fee waiver checking is only performed for accounts that are currently active (not dormant or closed).|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A10|4200-APPLY-MONTHLY-FEE|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:4200-APPLY-MONTHLY-FEE|When a monthly maintenance fee is applied, it is deducted directly from the account's balance.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A11|4300-WRITE-FEE-TRANSACTION|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:4300-WRITE-FEE-TRANSACTION|Every time a monthly maintenance fee is applied, a fee transaction record is created showing the account, the fee amount, the resulting balance, and the date.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A12|5100-UPDATE-DORMANT-COUNTER|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:5100-UPDATE-DORMANT-COUNTER|The account record keeps a running count of days since the last transaction, updated each processing cycle.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A13|7000-PRODUCE-CONTROL-TOTALS|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:7000-PRODUCE-CONTROL-TOTALS|At the end of each run, a control report is produced summarizing the total accounts processed, the number newly marked dormant, the number closed, and the number of monthly fees charged.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|

{note:title=Excluded as dead code}The following paragraphs exist in source but are never PERFORMed from ACCTMSTR's entry point, so no rules were extracted from them: 4700-LEGACY-OVERDRAFT-CHARGE, 4750-LEGACY-OVERDRAFT-NOTIFY.{note}

