h2. STMTGEN

*Coverage:* 7 / 7 reachable paragraphs processed (100.0%)

||Rule ID||Paragraph||Citation||Business Rule||Status||
|STMTGEN-A1|3000-PRINT-HEADER|src/STMTGEN.cbl:3000-PRINT-HEADER|Each customer statement begins with a header line showing the account identifier and the current account balance.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|STMTGEN-A2|4000-PRINT-TRANSACTIONS|src/STMTGEN.cbl:4000-PRINT-TRANSACTIONS|A statement lists only the transactions that belong to the account currently being statemented (i.e., transactions are matched to the account by account ID).|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|STMTGEN-A3|4000-PRINT-TRANSACTIONS|src/STMTGEN.cbl:4000-PRINT-TRANSACTIONS|Each listed transaction line on the statement shows the transaction type, the transaction amount, and the transaction date.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|STMTGEN-A4|5000-UPDATE-LAST-STMT-DATE|src/STMTGEN.cbl:5000-UPDATE-LAST-STMT-DATE|Whenever a statement is generated for an account, the account's last-activity date is updated to the current date, regardless of whether any customer transactions occurred during the statement period.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|

